Chapter: StarCatalog
  cites Starmap chapter CelestialTypes

 Catalog of named celestial objects. Real astronomical data from the
 HYG database (stars), Messier catalog (deep sky), and NGC catalog
 (galaxies, nebulae, clusters). Positions are galactic XYZ in parsecs
 scaled by 1000. Magnitudes scaled by 1000. B-V color index scaled
 by 1000.

Section: Star Builder Helpers

  mk-star : Integer, Text, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, SpectralClass, Text -> CelestialObj
  mk-star (id) (name) (x) (y) (z) (mag) (absmag) (bv) (sp) (con) =
    let base = co-new id name CkStar
    in let sized = co-set-dist base (star-dist x y z)
    in let placed = co-set-pos sized x y z
    in let bright = co-set-mag placed mag absmag
    in let tinted = co-set-color bright bv sp
    in co-set-constellation tinted con

  mk-dso : Integer, Text, CelestialKind, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Text, Text -> CelestialObj
  mk-dso (id) (name) (kind) (x) (y) (z) (mag) (con) (desc) =
    let base = co-new id name kind
    in let sized = co-set-dist base (star-dist x y z)
    in let placed = co-set-pos sized x y z
    in let bright = co-set-mag placed mag 0
    in let named = co-set-constellation bright con
    in co-set-desc named desc

 The far galaxies sit at 320,000,000,000 (parsecs x 1000), whose square is
 1.02e23 and does not fit a 64-bit integer, so the sum of squares has to be
 taken on scaled coordinates for them. 1,500,000,000 is the largest magnitude
 whose three squares still fit: 3 x 1.5e9 squared is 6.75e18 against a ceiling
 of 9.22e18. Everything nearer than 1.5 million parsecs, which is every star and
 every Messier object, takes the exact path.

  star-abs : Integer -> Integer
  star-abs (v) = if v < 0 then 0 - v else v

  star-widest : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  star-widest (x) (y) (z) =
    let a = star-abs x
    in let b = star-abs y
    in let c = star-abs z
    in let ab = if a > b then a else b
    in if ab > c then ab else c

  star-exact-limit : Integer = 1500000000

  star-isqrt : Integer -> Integer
  star-isqrt (n) = star-isqrt-loop n 0 3000000000

  star-isqrt-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  star-isqrt-loop (n) (lo) (hi) =
    if lo >= hi then lo
    else let mid = (lo + hi + 1) / 2
    in if mid * mid > n then star-isqrt-loop n lo (mid - 1)
    else star-isqrt-loop n mid hi

  star-dist : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  star-dist (x) (y) (z) =
    if star-widest x y z < star-exact-limit then star-isqrt (x * x + y * y + z * z)
    else star-dist-scaled (x / 1000) (y / 1000) (z / 1000)

  star-dist-scaled : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  star-dist-scaled (a) (b) (c) = star-isqrt (a * a + b * b + c * c) * 1000

